---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About — Field Notes">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="about-hero">
      <h1>About Field Notes</h1>
      <p class="handwritten">An open journal of the natural world</p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <p>
        <strong>Field Notes</strong> is a digital collection of observations from the natural world — field
        records, surveys, sketches, and quiet discoveries, shared openly with anyone who cares to read them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every note here began outdoors. A hawk crossing a river valley. The careful architecture of a dune
        grass community. The sound of insects on a June night. These are the small, specific moments that a
        naturalist carries home in a field bag, transcribed to paper while the details are still fresh.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Field observations</strong> — detailed records of species, behavior, and encounters in the wild.</li>
        <li><strong>Surveys & surveys</strong> — systematic notes on the plants and animals of a particular place.</li>
        <li><strong>Seasonal records</strong> — phenology, movement patterns, and the slow changes of the landscape.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Notes are written in the tradition of the field journal: dated, located, and recorded with enough
        detail that another person could return to the same place and find the same things.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Why public?</h2>
      <p>
        Observation is a shared practice. The notes of earlier naturalists — often collected over decades —
        remain a gift to those who follow. This journal is offered in the same spirit: a working record that
        anyone may read, use, and build upon. Whether you are a seasoned field observer or someone simply
        curious about the world outdoors, there is a place for you here.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Read the journal</h2>
      <p>
        The most recent observations live on the <a href="/">journal</a> page, newest first. Each entry
        records where it was made, when it was made, and what was seen.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="signature">
      <span class="sig">— The Field Notes contributors</span>
      <span class="stars">✦ ✦ ✦</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    text-align: center;
    padding: var(--space-3xl) 0 var(--space-xl);
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .about-hero h1 {
    font-size: 2.75rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .about-hero .handwritten {
    font-family: var(--font-handwritten);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--color-sepia);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .prose {
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    position: relative;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .prose h2::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 3rem;
    height: 2px;
    background: var(--color-sepia-light);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }

  .prose p {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-size: 1.075rem;
  }

  .prose ul {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    padding-left: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--color-accent-dark);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .signature {
    text-align: center;
    padding: var(--space-xl) 0 var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .signature .stars {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--color-sepia-light);
    opacity: 0.5;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .signature .sig {
    font-family: var(--font-handwritten);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-light);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .about-hero h1 {
      font-size: 2.2rem;
    }

    .prose {
      padding: 0 var(--space-md);
    }
  }
</style>